WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.693
A net is a two-dimensional arrangement of faces that folds into a solid. Count and

00:00:05.693 --> 00:00:06.792
position all faces.

00:00:07.617 --> 00:00:13.028
For the net of a rectangular prism, how many flat faces must be represented? The

00:00:13.028 --> 00:00:18.799
answer is 6. A rectangular prism has 6 faces, 12 edges, 8 vertices and two matching

00:00:18.799 --> 00:00:19.521
end faces.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:25.532
A child on a football field draws a flat net to fold a triangular prism. How many

00:00:25.532 --> 00:00:29.177
flat faces will the finished shape have? Pause to choose and explain.

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:35.684
A child on a football field draws a flat net to fold a triangular prism. How many

00:00:35.684 --> 00:00:41.003
flat faces will the finished shape have? The answer is 5. A triangular prism has 5

00:00:41.003 --> 00:00:44.327
faces, 9 edges, 6 vertices and two matching end faces.
